\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr/Late -2: Local Overnight Rates Soften \b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1997\par 11:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  A senior dealer at a \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank said the market remains 'wary' of MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although he believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been 'checking rates' rather than buying U.S. dollars actively. \par \par \uc2  The MAS, which doesn't comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities, has a policy of slowing any appreciation in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which it watches against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflecting Singapore's main trading partners. One dealer suggested the MAS has been buying dollars in small amounts through Thursday to check the U.S. dollar's slide. \par \par \uc2  Dealers put likely support for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around S$1.4250, with MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely to be heavy around S$1.4225. \par \par \uc2  Demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rubbed off on the local money market where overnight rates softened in particular, dealers said. 'A number of overseas parties have been long in U.S. dollars, and they are now unwinding (their positions),' one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rates for Singapore dollar deposits are at 2.5%-2.675% from 3.375%-3.5% in morning dealings. The three-month interbank rates are at 3.4375%-3.5625% from 3.625%-3.75%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0953GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6504357\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip