\par\par \b \uc2  Asian top 7  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves match G7 - Singapore. \b0\par\par\uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 30 (Reuter) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of the top seven Asian countries are equal to those of the Group of Seven industrialised nations, Singapore's Finance Minister Richard Hu told a conference on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The aggregate reserves of the top seven Asian countries matches that of the G7 countries," Hu told the annual conference of the International Securities Market Association (ISMA). \par \par \uc2  Hu's comments follow the recent speculative attack against the Thai baht in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) -- of which Hu is chairman -- \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Many Asian central banks have repurchase pacts between each other which enable them to defend another country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  using that country's holdings of U.S. Treasury securities as collateral. \par \par \uc2  Hu noted Singapore is the fourth most active \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading centre in the world. "Daily turnover in Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market averaged US$130 billion in 1996." \par \par \uc2  "Of this, only about six percent actually involved trading in the Singapore dollar," he added. \par \par \uc2  Turning to the prospects for Asia, Hu said the ongoing economic liberalisation in China, India and Indo-China is expected to unleash the next wave of economic growth in Asia. \par \par \uc2  "A recent World Bank study indicated that the Asian economies will expand at an average rate of 7.2 percent annually over the next 10 years, which is almost three times that of the industrialised countries," he said. \par \par \uc2  Hu said Asia's full growth potential can be realised only if there is efficient access to capital. \par \par \uc2  "Large infrastructure investments will cause demand for funds to exceed domestic savings in many countries. This will compel the Asian economies to look within and beyond the region for surplus capital," Hu said. \par \par \uc2  He said that over the next decade Asian financial markets will have to modify their traditional role of channelling funds from the developed economies. \par \par \uc2  "The key challenge for Asia in the next decade is therefore to sustain the healthy development of its financial markets, which is critical to fostering continued macro-economic growth of the region," he said. -- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5u04out\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
