\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Late-AM -2: Banque De France  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Rumored \b0\par\par\uc2 185 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 1997\par 06:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  There are strong rumors in the market that the Banque de France \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late morning \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading to support the French franc, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At 0430 GMT the mark is trading at FRF3.3755, down from around FRF3.3775 two hours ago, but still sharply up from its earlier level of FRF3.3650. \par \par \uc2  The French \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is looking to maintain the franc above FRF3.3775-FRF3.3780, according to a senior trader at a French bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is sharply higher on news of the French election results, trading at $1.6435 up from a low of $1.6370 against the dollar. Against the mark the U.K. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at DM2.7596, compared to DM2.7527 in earlier trading. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc also benefited from fears of a weaker French stance on monetary union, trading up to CHF1.3903 against the U.S. dollar from CHF1.3950, dealers said. The mark is at CHF0.8281, down from CHF0.8296 in earlier trading. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0455GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5q03ttq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
