\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Rupiah shrugs off campaign unrest. \b0\par\par\uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 1997\par 06:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 26 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah firmed in slow Monday morning trade despite news of widespread violence surrounding the country's election campaign. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the unrest on the last campaign day for the May 29 poll, which included the deaths of at least 142 people in the South Kalimantan capital of Banjarmasin, did not affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was quoted at 2,440.0/41.0 at 0405 GMT against an opening of 2,440.0/42.0. \par \par \uc2  "I suspect operators have gone long on the dollar in the spot market. They also have gone long in forwards," one dealer in Singapore said, adding that a U.S. public holiday was hampering trade as well. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said participants seemed to have factored in the risk of violence in the run-up to the general election, keeping the market relatively stable despite sporadic riots. \par \par \uc2  "I think operators are looking for good levels to sell," the dealer in Singapore said, adding that there was no reason for forwards to go higher because of cheap tom/next swaps. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. bank dealer in Singapore said the dollar was looking supported around 2,440.0 but its upside would be capped around 2,445.0/47.0 ahead of the election. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Thai baht had a very subdued morning as players in both domestic and offshore markets awaited the announcement of new monetary measures from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's press briefing, due to begin at 0400 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "Most players were reluctant to take new positions this morning as they are eagerly waiting for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new measures," a dealer at a foreign bank in Bangkok said. \par \par \uc2  Thai Bankers Association president Olarn Chaiprawat said on Sunday that he expected the Bank of Thailand (BOT) to give a strong signal for a domestic interest rate cut on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Olarn said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also likely to come up with new measures to formally separate the offshore and onshore \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The baht/dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has been informally divided into offshore and local markets since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to cut off offshore players' access to the baht when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under speculative attack almost two weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. bank dealer in Singapore said the offshore market was unlikely to be much moved by news of a cut in the BOT's discount rate, as interest in the baht had been severely dampened by the creation of a two-tier market. \par \par \uc2  In Malaysia, the ringgit firmed a few notches on the back of the dollar's drop against the mark, but activity remained largely subdued in the absence of fresh leads. \par \par \uc2  A European bank dealer in Singapore said the market was focusing on the French elections, where losses for President Jacques Chirac's coalition were causing a sell-off in the dollar/mark. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was good dollar buying interest from Kuala Lumpur parties around the 2.4990 ringgit level. \par \par \uc2  Further south, the Singapore dollar gained some ground from corporate selling of the U.S. dollar but fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped the domestic unit's rise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There was (U.S. dollar) selling interest from corporates from the 1.4310 level this morning and it touched a low of 1.4290/95 but local banks are still bidding around there," the U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support for the U.S. unit would limit its downside to around 1.4280 for the time being. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , typically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets through major local banks to stem any sharp moves in the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Madhav Reddy in KL (603-201 4813), Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221 384-6364), Anuchit Nguyen in Bangkok (662) 652-0642 and Sonali Desai in Singapore (65-8703090) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5q04yhh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
