\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  officials discuss the baht. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christopher Pizzey \par \uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 1997\par 12:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 25 (Reuter) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials met in Bangkok on Saturday and the top item on their agenda was the recent speculative attack against the Thai baht, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sources said on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand issued a one paragraph statement about the meeting which read in part, "The meeting has contributed to strengthening the cooperation among the central banks and monetary authorities in the region and enhancing the stability of the regional financial markets." \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders contacted by Reuters said it was obvious the main topic of conversation amongst the officials would have been the Thai baht. \par \par \uc2  "The meeting would have been a post mortem about the events of the week before last. They'll have looked at what they did right and what they did wrong," the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at a European bank in Singapore commented. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offcial from one of the banks attending the meeting declined to specifically say what had been discussed, but added, "Look at the timing and draw your own conclusion." \par \par \uc2  On May 14 and 15 the baht was the subject of a massive attack by speculators who had decided that the combination of a high current account deficit, economic woes and rumours of instability in the cabinet were good reasons to sell the baht. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand -- with the aid of other Asian central banks -- was able to fend off the attack. \par \par \uc2  Since the so-called 'Tequila Crisis' of 1994 when the Mexican peso was savaged by speculators, Asian central banks have been signing bilateral repurhase pacts between each other in which they agree to help defend their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against speculative attacks. \par \par \uc2  The first real test of these repurchase pacts came with the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's assault against the baht. \par \par \uc2  The usually secretive \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the baht while the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although not confirming it officially, was also highly visible in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said this weekend's gathering was part of the regular meeting of the Executives' Meeting of East Asia and Pacific (EMAP) Central Banks. \par \par \uc2  But the head of trading at the European bank said, "Regular it may be, but the location is a bit of a coincidence. They're sending a message to the speculators." \par \par \uc2  He added, "The message is pretty simple. It's along the lines of 'You're not taking Thailand on, you're taking all of us on.'" \par \par \uc2  The meeting was attended by senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials from Japan, Singapore, Malaysia, South Korea, Indonesia, China, Hong Kong and Thailand. \par \par \uc2  The head of Treasury at a U.S. bank in Singapore told Reuters he had not been aware of Saturday's meeting. "I think its hugely significant. They may say its under the auspices of EMAP, but...they would, wouldn't they." \par \par \uc2  "A lot these (central) bankers are worried that what happens to Thailand today could happen to them tomorrow. This sort of gathering of the clans will give them confidence," he added. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5p056ny\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
