\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Lower Vs U.S. Dollar In Early Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 1997\par 04:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is down against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trading Friday. \par \par \uc2  At 0200 GMT (10:00 p.m. EDT) the U.S. dollar is trading at S$1.4324, lower from its intraday high of S$1.4336, but above its S$1.4315 level in late trading Thursday. Traders say trading activity is brisk. \par \par \uc2  Traders attributed the Singapore dollar's fall to players buying U.S. dollars in response to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise against the yen since Tuesday from around Y112 to around Y116. \par \par \uc2  One head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a European bank based in Singapore said the Singapore dollar's next medium term move is likely to be upwards because the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to maintain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a level close to S$1.4300 against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The MAS, which doesn't comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities, has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to smooth any appreciation in the Singapore dollar, a direction which it prefers the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take to curb imported inflation. \par \par \uc2  Other traders said the Singapore dollar had drifted lower because of market participants covering short positions in the Malaysian ringgit. However, at 0200 GMT (10:00 p.m. EDT) the ringgit is at S$0.5724, marginally below its S$0.5728 level in late trading Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In the local money markets, short-term rates have risen slightly. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is at 3.875%-4.000%, higher from 3.750%-3.875% late Thursday. The three-month interbank rate is unchanged at 3.625%-3.750%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0228GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5n03m1i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
