\par\par \b \uc2  Southeast Asia Mkts Fall Seen Linked To Hedge Funds \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wong Wei Kong \par \uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 1997\par 13:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The recent heavy selling of Southeast Asian stocks is seen linked to foreign hedge funds that are also active in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, fund managers and dealers say Friday. \par \par \uc2  But while hedge funds sold regional stocks, Asian funds managed from within the region were mainly on the sidelines, say fund managers. \par \par \uc2  Asian markets tumbled Thursday after heavy speculative attacks on Thailand's baht Wednesday unsettled regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets. \par \par \uc2  The selldown sent regional benchmark stock indexes falling between 1.4% and 3.4% Thursday. Malaysia was worst hit, followed by the Philippines, two markets where there are the most concerns about a Thai-like situation developing. Thailand in recent years has become victim to overbuilding in the property sector that led to a slump that exposed its banks to bad loans. \par \par \uc2  Most Southeast Asian markets stabilized Friday in tandem with the retreat of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators, suggesting further that the activity of hedge funds in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets was linked, market watchers say. \par \par \uc2  'Who were the main sellers? U.S. hedge funds. We executed some orders for them,' says a dealing vice president at a European brokerage house. \par \par \uc2  'They might be shorting the markets at first. But later, they were selling stocks to fight the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  front. Hedge funds often leverage one instrument against the other,' he says. \par \par \uc2  After launching fierce attacks on the baht Wednesday, many hedge funds were stung Thursday when the Bank of Thailand jacked up short-term interest rates. The bank and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars for baht. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1121GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 62550 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5g03hwp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
