\par\par \b \uc2  Asian repo pacts seem to have survived first test. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christopher Pizzey \par \uc2 514 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 15 (Reuter) - The first real test of a series of agreements between Asian central banks to help each other defend their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to have been successful, economists and traders said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The symbolic importance (of the central banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) should not be understated. It's hugely significant," Desmond Supple, a senior analyst at BZW in Singapore, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht has been battered by huge sell orders in the last two days from investors and speculators concerned over the future direction of the economy and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But on Wednesday afternoon, the Bank of Thailand (BOT) and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , confirmed they had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the baht. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders reported that other Asian central banks such as the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  had also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the baht. But apart from the MAS, confirmation from other central banks was not forthcoming. \par \par \uc2  In the last 18 months, central banks in Asia have been signing up reciprocal repurchase agreements between each other. \par \par \uc2  The 'repo pacts' give participants instant access to cash for use to defend their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Under the pacts the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  receiving the assistance will put up U.S. Treasury securities as collateral. \par \par \uc2  "One's always wondered if these pacts actually mean anything. After yesterday I rather think they do," said the head of Treasury at a European bank in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amounts concerned were not necessarily the major factor. "The fact, that of all people, the MAS was prepared to ... be identified with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is crucial. They're being seen helping someone out," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Treasury head also noted the Bank of Japan had said it would be prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the financial markets to help support the baht if it were asked to by the Thai authorities. \par \par \uc2  "The agreement is there, although it is not a thing we would activate unless we were asked by Thailand," a Bank of Japan (BoJ) official told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "Here we've got the BoJ saying they'll defend the baht. Okay it's not with their own money, but when you've got the BoJ on your side is that helpful or not?" the Treasury head said. \par \par \uc2  BZW's Supple noted that even after news of the MAS's and the BOT's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had hit the market, some participants had continued to sell the baht. \par \par \uc2  But he added, "The market should realise they're not just taking on the Bank of Thailand." \par \par \uc2  Said the Treasury head; "Thailand's got over US$30 billion in its warchest. Under the repo agreements there's maybe another US$300-400 billion spare (cash) floating around." \par \par \uc2  He added; "These (repo) agreements make a difference. If the fundamentals are wrong, then fine, kick the hell out of the market. But if you're punting (speculating) then you have to accept you're taking on other central banks." \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore newsroom (65) 870-3080 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5f05np9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
