\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand says regional  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  supported baht. \b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par 14:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 15 (Reuter) - Several Asian central banks on Thursday cooperated with Thailand by jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the embattled baht against speculative attacks, Thai deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chaiyawat Wibulswasdi said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab    "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  obtained cooperation from several\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  central banks, including the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, today," Chaiyawat told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The deputy governor said speculative pressure against the baht eased substantially on Thursday and the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was mostly traded at 30-40 satangs below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's midrate of 25.81 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The baht was quoted sharply firmer at 25.250/25.350 late on Thursday against 25.910/25.940 early in the morning and 26.330/26.430 late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Thai and \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  central banks jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday to ward off heavy speculative pressure against the baht. Dealers estimated that the two banks had spent billions of dollars in shoring up the baht. \par \par \uc2  "Thais should not be carried away by rumours (in foreign markets)," Chaiyawat said referring to recent market concern over a sharply slowing Thai economy and speculation on a possible change of the Thai finance portfolio. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh has ruled out any change of his finance minister and key economic team. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said the baht's regained stability on Thursday was reflected by increased unwinding by speculators of long dollar positions. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rerngchai Marakanond said later on Thursday his bank agreed to buy over one billion dollars of dollar positions in the spot market, mostly at 25.30 baht to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought over one billion dollars in the spot market...to take profit," he said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5f05n48\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
