\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand/ \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2 /Central Banks-3: 1st Jt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 1997\par 10:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The sell-off in the baht Wednesday unnerved stock investors as well, causing the benchmark stock index to fall to a new six-and-a-half-year low. Around 0817 GMT, the Stock Exchange of Thailand index was down 33.38 points, or 5.6%, to 566.86 points. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand, in its joint statement, gave no details about the size of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The statement did not say whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been in the spot or forward markets. A spokeswoman for the Bank of Thailand declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, marks the first time Thailand's and \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's central banks have acted in concert, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said. Thailand has agreements with several central banks to cooperate in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crises, including those of Australia, Hong Kong, the Philippines, \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Malaysia and Japan. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped bring the dollar down from its high of 26.26 baht early Wednesday, but it wasn't sufficient to bring the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back within the band in which the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows it to trade against the baht. That means the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to continue spending money to defend the baht, and analysts expect the crisis to last several days. \par \par \uc2  The band was 25.84 baht to 25.88 baht Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  was hardly vigorous. 'The MAS isn't very aggressive in defending the baht,' one dealer said. 'They are quite mild.' Given Thailand's deteriorating economic health, he said, 'we don't think the central banks can do very much out of Singapore unless the fundamentals change.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0856GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5e03f8k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
