\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore dollar off highs as dlr/majors recover. \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 12 (Reuter) - The Singapore dollar remained firm but was off its morning highs in late Asian trade as the U.S. dollar made a partial recovery against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The domestic unit was quoted at 1.4340/50 to the U.S. dollar at 0830 GMT against its opening 1.4380/85. \par \par \uc2  It earlier rose to a near two-month high around 1.4300/05 in line with the U.S. dollar's steep drop to a four-month low of 117.50 yen. The dollar was at 118.51/61 yen at 0830 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "Basically the dollar/majors just recovered some of their losses," a European bank dealer said, adding that this had helped lift the dollar/Sing. \par \par \uc2  She said the U.S. dollar was likely to trade a 1.4330-1.4380 range against the Singapore dollar, with the 1.4400 level expected to pose stiff resistance for the next week at least. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said active buying of the U.S. dollar by local banks around its morning low spurred speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pushing the U.S. dollar back above the 1.4300 area. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  typically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets through major local banks to stem any sharp moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. It does not comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The local banks were buying dollars around the 1.4300/05. That's why it bounced up so fast to 1.4330/35," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  She said the U.S. unit should be supported around 1.4300 for the time being and players were likely to sell into any rallies towards the 1.4350 level. \par \par \uc2  "The market's still very long the dollar/Sing and ringgit/Sing cross so a lot of stop-losses were triggered," a U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5c05snc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
