\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Baht calms down after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 772 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 1997\par 07:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , May 9 (Reuter) - The Thai baht recovered from Friday morning lows by midday after the Bank of Thailand (BOT) denied market rumours of a band widening and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in spot and forward markets to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rumours, that the BOT planned to widen the dollar/baht trading band, emerged in London markets overnight and prompted a sell-off in the baht. \par \par \uc2  The baht was quoted at 26.013/26.018 to the dollar at 0510 GMT after the BOT \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to sell the dollar at 26.025 baht, dealers said. The Thai unit fell to to a low of 26.090 in early trade. \par \par \uc2  Paiboon Kittisrikangwan, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's division chief in charge of money and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, told Reuters the Bank of Thailand had no plan to change the exchange rate mechanism. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of U.S. investment houses were trying to attack the baht and buy dollars yesterday and it's been quite hectic today as well," said a U.S. bank dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's sharp drop against the majors on Friday also helped the baht rebound, but it was still trading well above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mid-rate of 25.99. \par \par \uc2  "People were reluctant to take many long dollar positions due to a weakening of the U.S. unit abroad and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," a dealer in Bangkok said. \par \par \uc2  But sentiment remained bearish and dealers said the baht could be vulnerable to further declines against the backdrop of continued weakness on the stock market and worries about the stability of the finance sector. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  benefitted from the dollar's sharp fall against the yen as fears of a rate hike in Japan gained ground while the likelihood of a further U.S. tightening appeared to recede. \par \par \uc2  A speech by Federal Reserve chairman Alan Greenspan late on Thursday was viewed as signalling that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might hold back from further rate hikes for the time being. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan said he expected economic growth to slow later this year and next, but that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would need to act if that did not prove to be the case. \par \par \uc2  "People took it as a sign that there won't be any immediate rate hike. That's why the market sold dollars and it has also turned quite bearish recently," a U.S. bank dealer in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 122.75/85 yen at 0510 GMT in Tokyo against its opening 123.15/18. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah rose amid steady money market liquidity though overall activity remained slow. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. bank dealer in Jakarta said the rupiah maintained a bid tone after strengthening to a high of 2,427.0 on Thursday in Singapore and New York while Jakarta was closed for a holiday. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was traded at 2,428.50/29.50 at 0510 GMT against an opening of 2,429.0/30.0. \par \par \uc2  A local bank dealer said the dollar briefly touched an early high of 2,430.0 before it was sold down on weakness in major offshore markets, where players brushed aside the heated campaign for Indonesia's general elections on May 29. \par \par \uc2  In Malaysia, the ringgit rebounded on the dollar's fall but a lack of participation kept it confined to a tight range. \par \par \uc2  "Ringgit sentiment for the short-term has changed due to weak dollar/majors," a dealer with a Malaysian bank said. "A lot of dollar selling is expected at above 2.5100." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the ringgit's upside could, however, be limited due to political concerns after Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad said he would grant full powers to his deputy Anwar Ibrahim and go overseas for two months later in May. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar showed signs of strengthening beyond the 1.4400 level against the U.S. dollar for the first time in more than three weeks. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/Sing could come off to 1.4380 depending on how far dollar/yen comes off. The market is still long dollar/Sing and ringgit/Sing," the U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said several stop-loss sell orders for the U.S. dollar appeared to be building below the 1.4410 level. The Singapore dollar was quoted at 1.4412/22 at 0510 GMT. \par \par \uc2  -- Syed Azman in Kuala Lumpur (603-206 2323), Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221-384-6364), Anuchit Nguyen in Bangkok (662-652-0642) and Sonali Desai in Singapore \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5905v3l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
