\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Ringgit hit by profit-taking. \b0\par\par\uc2 715 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 14 (Reuter) - The Malaysian ringgit saw another volatile session on Tuesday, coming under pressure as short-term speculators took profit on its recent sharp gains against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some funds were also looking at other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly the rupiah, for higher yield. \par \par \uc2  "The ringgit has risen by over two percent in one week. There has to be some profit-taking, correction," said the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing at a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  He said the ringgit was likely to consolidate around the 2.4850 region over the next few days. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit hit a 17-month high of 2.4660/70 a dollar on Monday against 2.5250 at the start of the year. It was at 2.4800/07 to the dollar at 0435 GMT. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the ringgit's overall uptrend remained intact as funds would continue to be attracted by the country's strong fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/ringgit came down quite rapidly over the new year and I think those who had gone short want to cover back because they're afraid the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might say it's been too rapid a rise for the ringgit," said a Japanese bank dealer in Singapore. He said players were likely to return to the ringgit towards the 2.4850-2.4900 levels. \par \par \uc2  Across the border, the Singapore dollar was stuck within a tight 1.4030-1.4060 trading band, despite some profit-taking in the ringgit/Sing cross. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the U.S. dollar looked supported around S$1.4030/40, where bidding by local banks had generated some talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , typically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets through major local banks. \par \par \uc2  But the Japanese bank dealer said 1.4040 was also a technical support level for the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah calmed down after a volatile overnight session, which saw it fall sharply in London markets on fears that a much-expected band widening would fail to materialise as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its fixing again on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said spot rupiah fell to a low of 2,383.0 in London overnight while others said the low was 2,379.0. \par \par \uc2  They attributed the sharp fall from Friday's low of 2,359.0 to stop-loss covering by offshore operators. \par \par \uc2  "Many offshore players were forced to cover because of the stop-loss limit. This triggered the sharp rupiah fall overnight," a U.S. bank dealer said in Jakarta said. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was quoted at 2,372.0/73.0 at 0435 GMT against an opening of 2,369.5/71.0. Its low was 2,374.0. \par \par \uc2  "The (dollar) shorts got nervous. And with Singapore and Jakarta closed in London time, there were only a couple of banks quoting five rupiah spreads for $10 million," said the Japanese bank dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  But he said the rupiah stabilised around the 2,368/73 region for the rest of the London session. \par \par \uc2  "From this morning, it just carried forward from the 2,370 level but 2,373.00/75.00 looks toppish at the moment," he said. "The band widening talk seems to have subsided." \par \par \uc2  Offshore operators started speculating heavily last Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was set to widen its band. \par \par \uc2  The speculation triggered heavy dollar selling because any band widening in the past had caused the rupiah to strengthen. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht slipped in line with the dollar's firmer tone against the majors, but dealers said its weakness was limited by some selling of the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The baht was quoted at 25.645-25.650 to the dollar at 0435 GMT against 25.630-25.635 late on Monday. The Bank of Thailand fixed the baht/dollar mid-rate at 25.66 against 25.65 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the overnight interbank rate could ease if dollar sales in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market persisted but demand for funds to meet value-added tax payments would prevent a sharp drop. \par \par \uc2  -- Madhav Reddy in Kuala Lumpur (603-230 8911), Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221-384-6364), Anuchit Nguyen in Bangkok (662) 652-0642 and Sonali Desai in Singapore (65-8703090) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt1e06bz9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
