\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW-UOB sees long way to "international" S$. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chris Johnson \par \uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 1996\par 06:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Dec 27 (Reuter) - The head of Singapore's United Overseas Bank Ltd (UOB), said on Friday he did not expect a speedy relaxation of rules curbing trading of the Singapore dollar on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  UOB chairman and chief executive Wee Cho Yaw told Reuters the Singapore economy was too small to allow active speculation in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I don't see any benefit to Singapore if the Singapore dollar is internationalised. I don't see the reason for it," Wee said in an interview. \par \par \uc2  UOB has a large treasury \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  which is active in a range of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  But, like its competitors, it is restricted by the size of Singapore dollar loans it can make and is discouraged by Singapore's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS), from speculating in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The MAS scrutinises all large trades in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to adjust its value. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister Richard Hu has said several times in the past year that he plans to gradually relax the rules on international trading of the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  He says he wants to boost the city-state as a regional centre for financial services and also encourage the trading of shares in foreign companies on Singapore's stock market. \par \par \uc2  But he has given no time frame for relaxing the rules and has not said how the MAS plans to do it. \par \par \uc2  Wee said the Singapore dollar, which has appreciated steadily against the U.S. dollar and most other major Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past few years, could be vulnerable to manipulation if it were traded freely on global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "The Singapore dollar market is so small, if someone manipulated the Singapore dollar I think it would be a big problem. We are not a big economy," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said he thought it would take a long time for the Singapore government to make any changes. \par \par \uc2  Asked how long it would take, Wee said: "I don't know. It is up to the government. But to me it is of no benefit at all." \par \par \uc2  Wee said UOB's treasury activities had suffered recently from volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "Over the past year I think our \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  business was not very good ... I think 1995 was the best. I think 1996 will be worse. There was more volatility in the (\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) market. People were reading it wrongly," he said, but declined to give details. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dscr01qjr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
