\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Baht seen pressured, ringgit off. \b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Sept 4 (Reuter) - Late European buying of Thai baht forwards after Asian hours on Tuesday pushed up forward rates in the three and six-months and will keep levels high Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is under pressure due to foreign investors' concern about the export growth Slowdown, political uncertainties and a widening current account deficit. \par \par \uc2  The gloomy mood was exacerbated by Moody's downgrade of Thai short-term sovereign ceiling ratings for bank deposits and other short-term obligations to Prime 2 from Prime 1. \par \par \uc2  "The Moody's downgrade sent jitters throughout Europe and we saw selling after hours from a German bank. That's why the forwards today are much higher than where Asia left it," said one dealer with a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the spot baht rate was steady at 25.309-25.312 to the dollar at 0520 GMT, versus 25.308-25.312 late on Tuesday on dollar's narrow movement abroad, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There was still little buying interest on the U.S. unit today despite the mounting tension in the Gulf," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the tightening liquidity and high short-term baht interest rates had prompted some dollar selling for the baht in the spot market this morning. \par \par \uc2  In Indonesia, the rupiah held steady following the release of the trade and inflation data for June and August respectively. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trade was relatively quiet despite the figures, which fell within market expectations. \par \par \uc2  Investors remained wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past few days to defend the lower end of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, bringing up dollar-rupiah levels, dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate by one point to 2,342/2,460 and the conversion rate also by one point to 2,342/2,388 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit, meanwhile, extended its fall against the dollar in morning Kuala Lumpur trading as players continued to buy back the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cover short positions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market shorted a lot of dollar recently and is now buying back," said one dealer with a foreign bank. "Market position is not favourable for the ringgit at the moment." \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9403e5r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
