\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Flat; Quick U.S. Dlr Rebound From Day Low \b0\par\par\uc2 230 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 1996\par 11:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is flat against its U.S. counterpart from early Asian dealings Thursday, after the U.S. dollar rebounded quickly from its intraday low of S$1.4060 around 0635 GMT amid rumors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) might have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they can't confirm any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but said fears that the MAS, \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , might be buying dollars, is one factor capping the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains. The MAS's stated policy is to curb any appreciation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, and it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this year to boost the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0840 GMT, the dollar was trading around S$1.4070, up from the intraday low of S$1.4060 at 0635 GMT, but lower from S$1.4071 at 0000 GMT early in Asian trading. \par \par \uc2  A spot dealer with one of the Singapore banks said the U.S. dollar also fell after a regional interbank player unwound some long positions against the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The fall in the U.S. dollar to the intraday low was helped by some selling in the Malaysian ringgit against the Singapore dollar, said several regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders. \par \par 