\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Steady After Early Rise Vs U.S. Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1996\par 08:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar has steadied against the U.S. dollar after kicking higher against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in speculative early Australian trading Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'The Sydney players started selling this morning, which triggered stop-losses in thin volumes,' a dealer with a U.S. investment bank said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar nevertheless looks well supported from buying above S$1.4060. \par \par \uc2  'Fears that the MAS (\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  (to buy U.S. dollars) is one factor, but there's nothing fundamentally to suggest the Sing' dollar should be much weaker,' a dealer with a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers put the U.S. dollar in a range of S$1.4060 to S$1.4120 for the near term. \par \par \uc2  Around 0630 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.4090, up from S$1.4084 in early Asian trading around 0000 GMT, but down from S$1.4105 in early Australian dealings, and from S$1.4108 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, local money-market rates are mixed. The overnight rate of Singapore dollar deposits is quoted at 3.625%-3.500%, down from 3.875%-3.750% Friday. The three-month interbank rate is up at 3.4375%-3.3125% from 3.375%-3.250% Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-08-96 \par \par \uc2  0640GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011017ds8q0028w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
