\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Exports/Amplifier -2: Little Boost For  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1996\par 11:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar did edge briefly higher after the release of the trade figures, as some players were expecting another month's worth of disappointing figures, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rally soon ran out of steam. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is at S$1.4117 in late Asian trading, up from a low for day of S$1.4096 around 0435 GMT after the trade figures were released, and from S$1.4102 in early Asian dealings around 0000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  'If the trade figures had been sharply worse than expected, then we would have seen heavy selling of the Sing' dollar,' said Ong Pang Liang, head of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Bank America. 'But the Singapore dollar remains fairly steady,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Economists said they see the July data having little impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's longer-term performance. \par \par \uc2  Fears in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the U.S. dollar and moderate any appreciation in the local unit is underpinning the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. \par \par \uc2  But its gains will be capped by the underlying strength of the Singapore economy, despite this year's slowdown. \par \par \uc2  'The Singapore dollar proves pretty resistant to monthly economic data - it's the trend which is important,' said Morgan Guaranty's Low. 'Singapore is still heading for a current account surplus of around 15% of gross domestic product this year, an amazing figure and one not to be sniffed at,' he added. \par \par \uc2  As for Singapore's trade performance for the rest of the year, economists said they aren't holding out for any unexpected boost for non-oil exports. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-08-96 \par \par \uc2  0935GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 55126 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds8k06r8y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
