\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Baht inches up in cautious market. \b0\par\par\uc2 689 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 19 (Reuter) - The Thai baht started the week on a slightly firmer note, helped by weekend comments by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor warning against speculative attacks on the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar buying has eased this morning with more interest in selling the U.S. unit," said a local bank dealer in Bangkok. "Players seem to be listening to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's warning against speculating on the baht on the weekend." \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand governor Rerngchai Marakanond said at the weekend the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the Thai baht if necessary. \par \par \uc2  He also said he was happy about the baht's current value and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to change its baht fixing policy this year. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar/baht trade was still cautious amid concern about the stability of the coalition government after last week's withdrawal of the third largest party. \par \par \uc2  The baht was quoted at 25.280-25.285 to the dollar at midday from 25.285-25.290 late on Friday. The Thai overnight interbank rate was steady at 11.00-11.50 percent in early trade. \par \par \uc2  In Indonesia, the rupiah was steady in thin trade as operators focused on the August 22 hearing of a lawsuit filed by Megawati Sukarnoputri, the ousted leader of the Indonesian Democratic Party (PDI), against the government. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. bank dealer in Jakarta said liquidity supply was a tight but the rupiah failed to strengthen due to demand for dollars. "There seems to be some strong customer demand this morning, which supported the dollar at the 2,341.5 level." \par \par \uc2  "Offshore operators are cautious due to the hearing of the lawsuit. But there was also some profit-taking from locals after they went short last week," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said overall the market appeared to be well balanced which had limited trading within a narrow range of only some 50 cents throughout the morning. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was quoted at 2,341.75/42.20 at midday, compared with an opening of 2,341.50/42.25. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit held up on light commercial buying but a dearth of fresh factors kept trade confined to a tight range. \par \par \uc2  "There's nothing happening in the market to move dollar/ringgit," said a foreign bank dealer. "But I think people are looking to buy ringgit on dips and this will limit its downside." \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said some overseas corporate bodies were waiting to sell between $500-$700 million in the next few days, which could take the ringgit back up to 2.4850 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was at 2.4920/30 to the dollar at midday against 2.4923/28 at close of Kuala Lumpur on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Across the border, the Singapore dollar shed some of its overnight gains but remained on firm ground on continued unwinding of long U.S. dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  A European bank dealer said dollar/Sing looked supported at 1.4075/80 initially and at the more solid level of 1.4055/60. But he said it was unlikely to rise above 1.4110 for the time being. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the presence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) had not been detected despite earlier expectations that the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's strength. \par \par \uc2  "This is a continuation of the liquidation of long (U.S. dollar) positions people built up over the last three weeks when the gloomy projections about Singapore's economy started to surface," said Andy Tan, economist at MMS International. \par \par \uc2  Tan said the Singapore dollar was also benefitting from weakness in the ringgit/Sing cross as interest rates softened in Malaysia. \par \par \uc2  He said the MAS could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar appreciating towards 1.4050 to the U.S. dollar, especially if the U.S. unit remained stuck in its present ranges against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -- Syed Azman in KL (603-230 8911), Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221-384-6364), Tang Nguyen in Bangkok (662-252-9950) and Sonali Desai in Singapore (65-8703080) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds8j045xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
