\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Political jitters weigh on baht. \b0\par\par\uc2 793 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  * Thai baht falls on offshore concern about stability of Thai government after third largest party in ruling coalition threatens to leave. \par \par \uc2  * Indonesian rupiah under pressure amid ample liquidity as overseas operators await political developments. \par \par \uc2  * Singapore dollar gives up some overnight gains as players turn wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support for U.S. dollar at S$1.4110/20. \par \par \uc2  * Malaysian ringgit continues decline on dollar short-covering and unwinding of ringgit/Sing positions. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 14 (Reuter) - The Thai baht fell prey to overseas concern about the stability of the Thai government on Wednesday after the third largest party in the ruling coalition threatened to leave the administration. \par \par \uc2  The baht fell to 25.289-25.292 to the dollar at midday from 25.275-25.278 late on Tuesday. The Bank of Thailand fixed the mid-rate at 25.27 to the dollar against 25.26 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "There are a lot of calls (from offshore) about the political situation," said a swap market dealer in Bangkok. "Buying (of forward dollars) is quite strong, but not panicky." \par \par \uc2  Meetings were being held on Wednesday morning to consider the future of Prime Minister Banharn Silpa-archa's government. \par \par \uc2  "There's been some buying of dollars out of U.S. houses in the morning but nothing much because Bangkok is not really reacting," said a Singapore-based dealer. He said some players in Bangkok felt Thailand would be better off with a different leadership due to the scandals plaguing Banharn's government. \par \par \uc2  Another Singapore dealer said she would favour selling dollar/baht on any moves up to 25.30/32, despite the political doubt, as Thai interest rates still offered an attractive yield. \par \par \uc2  Value added tax payments and outflows of foreign funds due to the uncertainty tightened domestic money market liquidity, pushing the Thai overnight interbank rate to 14.00-14.50 percent in early trade from 13.00-13.25 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In Indonesia, the rupiah lost some ground as local players sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid high liquidity. \par \par \uc2  "The falls are relatively small as foreign operators are not active yet due to worries of possible political uncertainties," said a Japanese bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 2,340.50/41.50 at midday, compared with an opening of 2,339.00/40.00. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign operators were awaiting outstanding police and court hearings in August involving Megawati Sukarnoputri, the ousted opposition leader of the Indonesian Democratic Party. \par \par \uc2  Megawati, who is to be questioned in connection with the recent riots in Jakarta, has filed a lawsuit against the government and the military for backing a rebel congress which ousted her as leader of the Indonesian Democratic Party. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar gave up some of its overnight gains as traders turned wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after London players pushed it to a high of 1.4115 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Even though dollar/Sing is looking soft, it's very tough to sell it at this level," said a European bank dealer, adding that the U.S. dollar was likely to hold above S$1.4110. \par \par \uc2  "This has always been the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level so the market gets wary when it reaches here," he said. \par \par \uc2  Although the presence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) had not been clearly detected, dealers said the market would be reluctant to push the Singapore dollar above its overnight high. \par \par \uc2  The MAS, \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , tends to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the U.S. dollar if the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar shows signs of appreciating too sharply. \par \par \uc2  "I would favour a sell on any uptick to the 1.4140 region to see it going lower to 1.4100/10," said another European bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Across the border, the Malaysian ringgit came under further pressure from continued unwinding of the ringgit/Sing cross and a lack of fresh buying incentives. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the slight fall in local interest rates was also making the ringgit less attractive, especially against the Singapore dollar. Players have favoured the cross for its yield in recent months. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was at 2.4950/55 to the dollar at midday against 2.4935/45 at close of Kuala Lumpur on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "I would buy dollar/ringgit on any dips for a test of the 2.4990 level," said a Singapore dealer, adding that this could provide a temporary cap to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  On the money market, interbank rates were mostly steady but remained under pressure ahead of fresh maturities which are expected to further expand liquidity. \par \par \uc2  -- Syed Azman in KL (603-230 8911), Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221-384-6364), Tang Nguyen in Bangkok (662-252-9950) and Sonali Desai in Singapore (65-8703080) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds8e049lp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
