\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Baht calms down as rates soften. \b0\par\par\uc2 718 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  * Thai baht firm but activity subdued as domestic interest rates subside following \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures to ease liquidity. \par \par \uc2  * Indonesian rupiah holds steady but seen rising as confidence returns among offshore investors. \par \par \uc2  * Malaysian ringgit lacks direction in thin market ahead of May trade data. \par \par \uc2  * Singapore dollar stays encased in recent range as players remain wary of pushing it higher. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 2 (Reuter) - The Thai baht remained on solid ground but saw limited interest on Friday as domestic interest rates subsided from their recent heady levels. \par \par \uc2  The Thai overnight interbank rate was steady at 13.00-14.00 percent in early trade after falling sharply from Thursday's high of 25.00-26.00 percent following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's measures to ease tight liquidity. \par \par \uc2  "The money supply continues to improve this morning. There are more banks offering funds in the market," said a local bank dealer in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand injected 10 billion baht into the system through the bond repurchase market and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in swap markets in Hong Kong and \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bring down swap interest rates on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it would allow finance firms and banks to borrow funds from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  through guaranteed instruments in the repurchase market. \par \par \uc2  The bank previously only accepted government and state enterprises' bonds as guarantees for borrowing in the bond repurchase market. \par \par \uc2  Liquidity had come under intense pressure in Thailand due to heavy outflows of foreign funds following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's downward revision of its 1996 growth forecast last week. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a Singapore-based bank said there had been no sign of Bank of Thailand \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the swap market on Friday. "People already sold everything yesterday. Once the market has cooled off, I don't think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would come in," she said. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah held steady as fears of the recent political turmoil fade, prompting expectations of a renewal of overseas investor confidence. \par \par \uc2  "Offshore operators seem to be reducing dollar holdings. Some may start to establish short dollar positions," said a dealer in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 2,343.25/44.25 at midday, compared with an opening of 2,345.0/47.0. Its high was 2,342.75. \par \par \uc2  A European bank dealer said the dollar was well supported at 2,340.0 and some operators were seen trying to break the 2,342.0 support level but had failed. \par \par \uc2  "Operators are also looking at this weekend. If nothing major happens, I think we are going to see the rupiah strengthening further," another foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta was calm on Friday morning although troops were still seen guarding strategic points in the city in the wake of last weekend's riots. \par \par \uc2  The stock and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets made a strong recovery on Thursday after fears of a confrontation between troops and opposition activists eased. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit continued to track narrow ranges, showing no clear direction in a thin market as players awaited May trade data. \par \par \uc2  "There is virtually nothing happening. No one seems to know what will really move the market," said the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing with a foreign bank in Kuala Lumpur. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said it was widely believed Malaysia would report a trade deficit for May this year. \par \par \uc2  "The trade figures may provide some excitement, but going by past trend, it may be a 'sell on rumour, no action on fact' situation," a dealer with a European bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  Across the border, the Singapore dollar was similarly afflicted by a lack of interest. But dealers said the U.S. dollar would remain well supported at S$1.4130 partly due to a perception that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would support that level. \par \par \uc2  "In the past few days, the market went there (the 1.4130 level) and bounced up very fast," said a dealer with a European bank. She said Singapore authorities were likely to stem an appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to signs of slower economic growth following an unexpected decline in June non-oil exports. \par \par \uc2  She said dollar/Sing would remain well contained in a range of 1.4130 and 1.4170 for the day. \par \par \uc2  -- Madhav Reddy in KL (603-230 8911), Mantik Kusjanto in \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds8204mf6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
