\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Trapped In Narrow Range Vs U.S. Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 229 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 1996\par 10:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar remained trapped in a narrow range against the U.S. dollar Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was at S$1.4045 around 0845 GMT, having traded in a range of S$1.4045 to S$1.4047 during Asian dealings. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at S$1.4048 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  'Nothing has been going on to move the market today,' said a senior trader at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  'They're lots of orders (to sell U.S. dollars) around S$1.4070, but everyone is nervous that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  below S$1.4040,' he added. That explained the U.S. dollar's tight ranges against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), the country's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  a number of times this year to support the U.S. dollar against the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit was at S$0.5641, down from S$0.5649 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 3.250%-3.125%, from 2.250%-2.375% late Thursday. The 3-month interbank rate was at 2.375%-2.250% against 2.3125%-2.1875%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-05-96 \par \par \uc2  0846GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds5a03y33\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscal