\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Flat Vs U.S. Dlr: Trading Range Tight \b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 1996\par 11:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar drifted sideways to settle little changed against the U.S. dollar from levels in early Asian dealings in quiet late trading Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Short-covering by interbank players briefly picked the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  off its intraday lows against the Singapore unit, but the U.S. dollar kept to a 30-point range for the day, a trader with a U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  'The market is still long (on the Singapore dollar) and we might see the (U.S.) dollar test support at S$1.3970 when stop losses could send it lower,' he said. \par \par \uc2  But that would most likely trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), which has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market a few times this year to curb the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness against the Singapore dollar, the trader added. \par \par \uc2  Traders said a slight weakening in the Malaysian ringgit against the Singapore dollar was not significant. \par \par \uc2  'The market's just dithering ahead of the release of the Malaysian trade deficit figures,' a trader with another U.S. bank said. The Malaysian government has confirmed the February trade balance will be in deficit but hasn't given details. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was at S$1.4043 around 0914 GMT, up a touch from S$1.4040 in early Asian trading around 0000 GMT, and from S$1.4039 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was at S$0.5631 against S$0.5626 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 2.000%-1.875%, from 2.375%-2.250% late Monday. The 3-month interbank rate was at 2.250%-2.125% from 2.3125%-2.1875%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-05-96 \par \par \uc2  0913GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds5703qkn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
