\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Ringgit ranges, market awaits data. \b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  * Ringgit rangebound but volatility expected as traders await Malaysia release of key February trade data in afternoon. \par \par \uc2  * Singapore dollar seen capped at 1.4000 to dollar where market pegs next \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  * Baht edges up in profit-taking after Friday panic sales. \par \par \uc2  * Dollar-rupiah trades to bottom of band on tight rupiah liquidity. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 7 (Reuter) - Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were traded moderately in the morning but the dollar-ringgit is poised for a volatile afternoon with the release of key trade data today. \par \par \uc2  Malaysian Finance Minister and Deputy Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim told reporters on Tuesday that the country had chalked up a trade deficit in February but added the actual figure would be released when Parliament meets this afternoon. \par \par \uc2  "We've seen a pretty good range of trading in the dollar-ringgit this morning, but everyone is waiting for the numbers," said one dealer with a U.S.bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have been speculating on a figure of between 500 million and 1.5 billion ringgit after 1.1 billion in January. \par \par \uc2  "Anything outside these figures could see the market move either way," said a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with a U.S. bank in Singapore. At 0430 GMT, the ringgit was trading at 2.4935/45. \par \par \uc2  But another dealer in Singapore said, "Whatever the figure, the market seems to have largely discounted it. It is a buy on rumour, sell on fact situation." \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Thai baht firmed in early trade on the back of tight liquidity but market expectations are for heavy buying of dollars from the Bank Of Thailand to tighten liquidity and dollar demand from offshore players. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said, however, the baht, which fell on Friday following comments from a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official about the standing practice of pegging it to a fixed dollar-denominated basket of curencies, will remain under pressure. \par \par \uc2  "There's still concern over the official's comment," said a dealer with a U.S. bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah fluctuated against the dollar in active early trading, dealers said, adding that tight liquidity caused offloading of value-today dollars. \par \par \uc2  One European bank dealer said the downside of the dollar appeared to be limited because it was already at the lower end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's floor rate. \par \par \uc2  "Should the dollar-rupiah dip below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's floor rate, we can expect bank Indonesia to flood the market with rupiah funds,' said one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist's report. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar remains capped at the 1.4000 level against the U.S. dollar, pressured by market expectations for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying at the level. \par \par \uc2  "For today resistance should be 1.4020/25," said one economist, adding, however, that the MAS may shift its preferred U.S.-Singapore dollar fluctuation band to a highe level at 1.4020/25. \par \par \uc2  -- Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221-384-6364), Tang Nguyen in Bangkok (662-252-9950) and Valerie Lee in Singapore (65-8703080). \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds5708da1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
