\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore will not use  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  to boost exports. \b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 29 (Reuter) - Singapore, which sees exports growing as robustly this year as in 1995, will not need to manage its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stimulate its export market, finance minister Richard Hu said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In a wide-ranging interview with Reuters Financial Televison, Hu said the contribution of exports to Gross Domestic Product in 1995 was 66 percent, "a shade lower than in 1994." \par \par \uc2  He said that in 1996 the export contribution will be "similarly strong." \par \par \uc2  "Given we don't see a problem of a decline in exports, there is no need to utilise...an exchange rate stimulus," Hu said, speaking just before the launch of RFTV in Singapore on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Hu said Singapore has a completely open economy without capital and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls, and any attempt to keep the Singapore dollar artificially weak to sustain export growth would result in price and wage inflation. \par \par \uc2  "Our policy is to maintain sustainable growth with low inflation," he said, adding that monetary policy has been successful over the last decade and the Singapore dollar has appreciated against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the period. \par \par \uc2  "In particular against the US dollar we have appreciated 33 percent," Hu said. \par \par \uc2  The finance minister said Singapore's policy was also not to manage the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support any particular sector of the economy. \par \par \uc2  "(The Singapore dollar) has been floating since we lifted all \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls in 1978. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  periodically in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to erase any spikes in exchange rates," Hu said. \par \par \uc2  Hu said Singapore is unlikely to be adversely affected by the growth of other financial centres regionally as it is a "sophisticated financial centre with a full range of sophisticated financial products". \par \par \uc2  In a speech at the launch of RFTV, Hu said as at the end of February this year, 142 commercial banks and 79 merchant banks were operating in Singapore while 20 new fund managers started \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  here, bringing the total number to 140. \par \par \uc2  Hu said Singapore's financial industry grew by 7.3 percent in 1995 against 1994. \par \par \uc2  The republic's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market grew by 43 percent in daily average volume terms to US$105 billion, maintaining Singapore's position as the fourth largest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the world. \par \par \uc2  Hu said fund managers in Singapore managed total funds of Singapore $90 billion in 1995, an increase of 37 percent over the S$66 billion in 1994 while the total amount of loans syndicated grew by 15 percent to S$11.5 billion in 1995 from S$10 billion in 1994. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore minister said the location of Reuters regional \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Singapore was an important contribution to the development of the city state as an international financial centre. \par \par \uc2  He said presently 23 news wire agencies and 19 foreign television, radio and satellite broadcasters have set up bases in Singapore. -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds3t09t45\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\sh