\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Wallows In Tight Range Vs U.S. Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 248 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 09:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar wallowed in a narrow trading range against the U.S. dollar Monday, dipping slightly from intraday highs in late trading. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at S$1.4065 around 0805 GMT, up from an intraday low of S$1.4063 around 0444 GMT, but down from S$1.4070 at its Asian opening. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading volumes were thin, with the market looking ahead to Taiwan's presidential election March 23 and its impact on the strained relations with China. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a German bank said 'big banks have just been playing around inside the trading range' for both the U.S. dollar and Malaysian ringgit against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'The Singapore dollar is not moving anywhere,' he said. Dealers said the market is still wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around S$1.4050 after the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was quoted at S$0.5538, up slightly from S$0.5537 in early Asian dealings. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 2.165%-2.000%, from 2.500%-2.375% at about the same time Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The 3-month interbank rate was at 2.3125%-2.1875% from 2.250%-2.125%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NE