\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Stronger; Inflow Of HK, Taiwan Funds \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 09:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is stronger against its U.S. counterpart from early Asian dealings Wednesday and is likely to remain strong in short-term dealings, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  The reason why the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is strong and short term rates low is because a lot of Hong Kong and Taiwan accounts have parked their funds here, said a senior dealer at a Singapore bank. There has been a fairly big inflow amid the escalating tensions between China and Taiwan. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market tends to view the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a safe haven and values its stability. Other key beneficiaries from the China-Taiwan tension Wednesday include the Australian and New Zealand dollar. \par \par \uc2  Another trader at a Singapore bank said the short-term bearish outlook on the U.S. dollar against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also contributing to the strength of the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said there are worries about pushing the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  much higher for fear that the country's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might support the U.S. dollar around S$1.4050-60. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is known to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets from time to time, using it as a tool to check domestic inflation. \par \par \uc2  Around 0800 GMT, the dollar was trading around S$1.4072, from S$1.4082 early in Asian trading and from S$1.4079 at about the same time on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 1.750%-1.625%, from 1.750%-1.625% at about the same time Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The 3-month interbank rate was at 2.1875%-2.0625%, from 2.1875%-2.0625%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-03-96 \par \par \uc2  0814GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3d028uk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
