\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Shares End -2: Fels, Comfort, ICS Close Higher \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 1996\par 10:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  One feature was Far East Levingston Shipbuilding (Fels) Ltd. which attracted good demand to close up 25 cents at S$8.25. \par \par \uc2  The upswing in Fels reflected growing confidence about a possible recovery in the international oil market and exploration spending in 1996 which would benefit demand for the company's offshore drilling rigs and related equipment, a trader with a European stockbrokers said. \par \par \uc2  Among other gainers, taxi operator Comfort Group Ltd. touched a new 14-month high of S$1.37, before easing to close at $1.35 in active trading, with 8.05 million shares changing hands. The company is in favor because it has lagged the market's overall gains in recent weeks, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Property group Insurance Corp. of Singapore Ltd. rose 24 cents to $4.46 in what one trader at a local stockbrokers said was good demand from a U.K. institutional buyer. He said the company should report good earnings shortly, while the value of its portfolio of prime commercial property is on the rise. \par \par \uc2  Under continued pressure were the foreign stock of banks, with Oversea-Banking Corp. Ltd. and The Development Bank of Singapore Ltd. down 50 cents and 20 cents respectively at $19.80. \par \par \uc2  A trader with a local stockbrokers said U.K. and Hong Kong institutions have been lightening their holdings of the stocks which have been commanding 'unjustifiably high foreign premiums'. \par \par \uc2  Total market volume was 126.7 million units valued at S$347.9 million. A total of 275 stocks closed higher, 66 lower, while another 197 ended unchanged. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar ended late-Asian trading at S$1.4089 around 0900 GMT, up from its Australasian opening of $1.4070. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), the country's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , boosted the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early local trading against the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-02-96 \par \par \uc2  0945GMT \par \par \uc2  5012 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2n01mtb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
