\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Lower After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  and U.S. Dlr Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 1996\par 09:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AP-Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is lower Friday after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authorities and the U.S. dollar's rise against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said traders. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore buying the U.S. dollar at S$1.4060 in early Friday trading. They said this was seen as a signal to the market that the dollar should trade closer to the S$1.4100 level. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a U.S. bank said the dollar's rise against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  boosted the sentiment on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the Singapore dollar. The dollar bounced up from an intraday low of 104.47 yen to above 105.00 on reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar is likely is likely to meet very strong resistance at S$1.4090 and further at S$1.4120. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT, the dollar was trading around S$1.4080, up from S$1.4070 early in Asian trading and from S$1.4055 at about the same time Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 0.875%-0.7500%, from 1.500%-1.375% at about the same time Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The three-month interbank rate was at 2.125%-2.000%, from 2.250%-2.125%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-02-96 \par \par \uc2  0856GMT \par \par \u