\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore dealers shrug off  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  pact with BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 1996\par 11:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Feb 22 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Hong Kong's pact to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on behalf of the Bank of Japan (BOJ) will boost \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity in both centres but do little to keep speculators at bay, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "It will be effective for a while. Then the market will get smart to it and realise it's basically all from the same source. These days there's nobody too big for the market," said a U.S. bank trader. \par \par \uc2  "It's been greeted with disappointment, mainly because it doesn't represent any new fund of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Sim Moh Siong, economist at consulting firm I.D.E.A. \par \par \uc2  He said, however, the agreement would boost liquidity in Singapore and Hong Kong as both central banks would be drawing on BOJ reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Japan's behalf. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a British bank said the agreement was no different from similar pacts between the Bundesbank and the Federal Reserve, and the BOJ's own agreements with other central banks. \par \par \uc2  "I think they are trying to talk the market up. The danger is that people will rely on it," he said, noting that players could end up holding on to dollars when there was no fundamental reason to buy them. \par \par \uc2  He said the agreement was in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's policy against a sharp appreciation of the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  A senior Bank of Japan official said in Tokyo on Tuesday Japan's decision to ask other Asian monetary authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on its behalf was not aimed at halting the strengthening of the yen. \par \par \uc2  He said Japanese, Singaporean and Hong Kong authorities started discusssing cooperative ties last year and decided last week to make the announcement on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2m018u2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
