\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Dlr/Singapore Dlr -2: Range Of S$1.4000-70 Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 220 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 1996\par 04:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with Technical Data of Thomson Singapore said the strength of the Singapore dollar stemmed from the recent tie up between the Bank of Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore. A deal Tuesday will enable the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities to help their Japanese counterparts to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the dollar against the Japanese yen on their behalf. \par \par \uc2  He said the market interpreted the move as authorities trying to unwind some of the positions in the dollar against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and support the dollar against the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  He said some Japanese banks were noted selling the dollar against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, the dollar is seen holding between S$1.4000 and S$1.4170 in short term dealings. Dealers said the dollar continues to carry a slightly bearish tone against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , mainly because of the bearish sentiment on the dollar in general. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 1.500%-1.375%, from 4.250%-4.000% at about the same time Friday. \par \par \uc2  The 3-month interbank rate was at 2.250%-2.125%, from 2.375%-2.250%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-02-96 \par \par \uc2  0345GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2m01lbi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\