\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Dlr Flat Vs. Singapore Dlr; Seen In Thin Ranges \b0\par\par\uc2 218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 1995\par 09:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar has hardly changed against the Singapore dollar from early Asian dealings Friday, after staying in a thin 9-point range. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the lackluster sentiment on the dollar against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to persist as it stayed in the familiar range of S$1.4110 to S$1.4150. \par \par \uc2  Market players said they are reluctant to sell the dollar below S$1.4100 for fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authorities. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was seen recently buying the dollar at S$1.4080-85. Its presence was not noted Friday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, sell orders are known to exist at S$1.4150, said traders. \par \par \uc2  Around 0750 GMT, the dollar was trading around S$1.4115, from S$1.4123 early in Asian trading and from S$1.4117 at about the same time on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 2.500%-2.375%, from 2.125%-2.000% at about the same time Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The 3-month interbank rate was at 2.6875%-2.5625%, from 2.6875%-2.5625%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-11-95 \par \par \uc2  0804GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbo09at0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
