\par\par \b \uc2  S'pore dollar rise capped by  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  -- dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 10 (Reuter) - Gains in the Singapore dollar are seen capped at 1.41 to the U.S. dollar in the near term due to fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was at 1.4112/22 against its U.S. counterpart at the close of local trading on Friday compared with the opening of 1.4107/12. \par \par \uc2  The local dollar remained trapped in a very tight range against the U.S. dollar during Asian trading despite the greenback's weakness against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the S$1.41 level is seen as a crucial support for the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. bank dealer said the MAS was believed to have bought the U.S. dollar when it fell to S$1.4095 in New York earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  The MAS, Singapore's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traditionally does not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "As long as dollar/yen remains above 100, I think they might still continue to provide support at 1.41," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  A European bank trader said the MAS was unlikely to try to push for a higher U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "It is just a smoothening process. They don't want people to get too speculative on either side," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  He said the U.S. dollar's topside is seen at around S$1.42 for the time being. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the MAS was expected to give up the support level of S$1.41 if the U.S. dollar drops below 99 yen. \par \par \uc2  "If the dollar is really coming down in a big way, I don't think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  here will go against market forces," said another European bank trader. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar hit a record high of 1.3912 earlier this year. -- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drba01y0s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
