\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Dlr Down Vs. Singapore Dlr Despite MAS Buys At S$1.4210 \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 1995\par 09:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar is lower against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar from early Asian dealings Wednesday, despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authorities earlier at around S$1.4210, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS), the country's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was seen actively buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at S$1.4210 around Singapore's midday lunch break, said traders. \par \par \uc2  But bearish sentiment on the dollar against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still seen damping the tone of the U.S. dollar against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said dealers. As long as the dollar is below 100.00 yen and 1.4200 Deutsche marks, it is going to depress the U.S. dollar against the Singapore dollar, said a dealer at a Singapore bank. \par \par \uc2  Market players said that the Malaysian ringgit is likely to stay in ranges against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term, after big swings both ways since last week. The ringgit is seen holding between S$0.5600-40 in the short term, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  At 0700, the ringgit was quoted at S$0.5629. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar is seen holding between S$1.4180 and S$1.4225 in short term dealings, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  Around 0700 GMT, the dollar was trading around S$1.4207, from S$1.4250 early in Asian trading and at about the same time on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on the Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 3.250%-3.125%, unchanged from about the same time Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The 3-month interbank rate was at 3.000%-2.875%, from 3.0625%-2.9375%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-10-95 \par \par \uc2  0729GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drai085l0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
