\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Survey -4: Volume Below Expectations \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 1995\par 17:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The volume was below the expectations of many market observers, some of whom had even expected Singapore to overtake Tokyo as the busiest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  center in Asia. Senior bank executives said the MAS has been citing a figure of U.S.$110 billion as the average daily volume for 1995 up to July. \par \par \uc2  But the Bank of Japan's survey, also released Tuesday, showed Tokyo still far in the lead, with 34% volume growth pushing its turnover to U.S.$161.4 billion in April 1995. \par \par \uc2  In advance of the figures, some traders and economists in Singapore said they were wary of the survey representing the markets accurately because of its timing. Most of the Asia-based trading in the U.S. dollar against the Japanese yen takes place in Tokyo, and the dollar sank to its post-World War II low against the yen during that period amid heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders noted. \par \par \uc2  Traders also noted that \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a more diversified market. In its 1994-95 annual report, the MAS reported that dollar-mark and dollar-yen transactions made up 27% and 23% respectively of the market's total volume. And senior market observers now estimate that trading in the 'regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' - primarily the Malaysian ringgit, Thai baht and Indonesian rupiah - makes up about 20% of market turnover. \par \par \uc2  Speaking before the MAS release on Tuesday, Y.S. Wong, the head of regional financial markets for Citibank in Asia-Pacific, said that, regardless of the volume data, he views Singapore as Asia's most vibrant market. \par \par \uc2  'Singapore no doubt right now is the most active - I don't know about the largest - interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  center in Asia, no question about it.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-09-95 \par \par \uc2  1515GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9j078w5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
