\par\par \b \uc2  S'pore will slow its dollar's rise when necessary. \b0\par\par\uc2 207 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 7 (Reuter) - Singapore will act to slow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise when necessary, but its basic value is determined by the market, a government minister said. \par \par \uc2  Trade and Industry Minister Yeo Cheow Tong told Parliament: "The Singapore dollar will continue to increase as long as we continue to have strong economic growth...The private sector should bear this in mind when planning business \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Yeo said the value of the Singapore dollar is determined by the international \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. "It would be impossible for the Singapore government to artificially set the value of the Singapore dollar." \par \par \uc2  Yeo said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  "will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow down the pace of the increase when necessary." \par \par \uc2  He said that in the first five months of this year, the Singapore dollar has appreciated by 11 percent against the U.S. dollar but depreciated by five percent against the yen and six percent against the Deutschemark year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  He said the government is making a study on the impact of the appreciation of the Singapore dollar on different industries, which will be completed in several months. \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr77064a4\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cell